# Agent session artifacts. The Playwright MCP writes screenshots, console logs
# and accessibility snapshots into the working directory as it drives the app.
# They are session debris, not sources — the prototype they were taken from
# lives on `prototype/rank-distribution`.
.playwright-mcp/

# Machine-local Claude Code settings: permissions granted on this machine only.
# The shared configuration is `.claude/settings.json`.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Findings files from `/fan-out`, read back by `/counter-check`. They are a
# session artifact about branches under review, not source: the moment those
# branches merge, the file describes a state that no longer exists. What
# survives a review belongs in the PR, the ticket or an ADR.
review/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# JetBrains IDE project files. Machine- and user-specific: deployment targets,
# module paths, local PHP interpreter.
.idea/

# There is no build step (ADR 0004) and the core runs under `node --test`
# without packages, so this directory should never appear. If it does,
# something pulled in a dependency and that is a decision, not a side effect.
node_modules/

# Playwright writes screenshots to the CWD when a bare filename is given,
# not into .playwright-mcp/. One slipped into #96 that way.
*.png
!docs/**/*.png
!public/apple-touch-icon.png

# Deploy connection data for `./deploy.sh`: host, port, path. No secrets —
# authentication is by SSH key — but it is machine-local, like
# `.claude/settings.local.json`. The tracked template is `.env.deploy.example`.
.env.deploy
